    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n62004" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">λᾰσῐαύχην</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ενος</span>,
			ὁ, ἡ, (<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">λάσιος</span>) <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>with rough, shaggy neck</i>, of the centaur, <i><span class="en">
				<u>h.Merc.</u>
				224
			</span></i>, cf. 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">λασιαύχενα χαίταν</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Ar.
					<u>Ra.</u>
					822
				</span></i>
			 (lyr.); of the bear, <i><span class="en">
				<u>h.Hom.</u>
				7.46
			</span></i>; of the horse, <i><span class="en">
				S.
				<u>Ant.</u>
				350
			</span></i> (lyr.); 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">λ. βύρσα</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Theoc.
					25.272
				</span></i>
			: also with a neut., <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">λασιαύχενος
				ἄντρου</span>
			v.l.
			<i><span class="en">
				Id.
				<u>Ep.</u>
				5.5
			</span></i>.</div>
